      "math_academy_id": "q-181958",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Which of the following is a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times B$ for $A=\\{p,q\\}$ and $B=\\{w,z\\}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $B$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/6baae52e45d00d31eac732a23be655b648765c27cfcdc667c511b176d5bbbc88.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B.$\n\nOur completed $A\\times B$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14123139/assets/38e9d12b0c09ae066149d95235a6918712214edc147c57775da2d880b584cb9e.png)",
